Package: groundtruth
Title: Simulation Studies for Gaussian, Logistic, and Random-Intercept Models
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: person("Shinichi", "Nakagawa", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "snakagaw@ualberta.ca")
Author: Shinichi Nakagawa [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Shinichi Nakagawa <snakagaw@ualberta.ca>
Description: Generate independent Gaussian, Bernoulli-logit, and Gaussian
    random-intercept data, compare fitting adapters on paired observations, retain
    every fit attempt, replay recorded random streams, and export data with
    provenance. Summaries report target recovery, Monte Carlo uncertainty, and
    interval coverage with explicit failure denominators. Random-intercept
    variance targets use maximum-likelihood or restricted maximum-likelihood
    estimates without variance intervals.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: stats, digest, parallel, tools
Suggests: lme4, testthat (>= 3.0.0), roxygen2, pkgdown
Config/testthat/edition: 3
URL: https://itchyshin.github.io/groundtruth/, https://github.com/itchyshin/groundtruth
BugReports: https://github.com/itchyshin/groundtruth/issues
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.0.0
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
